       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's long half-life of 30 to 50 hours would prolong the effects. Normal kidney and liver function don't change this.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, if you want a lower dose for a frail patient or one on other antihypertensives\n\nIf you do intend 50 mg, please confirm that, ideally with the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
